# Critical Development Rules

Apply these rules in every implementation and refactor.

## Root Mounting (mandatory)

- Never keep a generic root id like `microfrontend-root` for new resources
- Use `<div id="{resource-name}-root"></div>` in `index.html`
- Keep `document.getElementById("{resource-name}-root")` in `src/main.tsx` aligned
- Treat id mismatch between `index.html` and `main.tsx` as blocking issue

## Parameter Validation (mandatory)

- Never trust optional inputs from props, URL/query, events, or API payloads
- Add guard clauses/early returns before using values
- Use Zod schema validation for external/untrusted data whenever possible
- Document expected invalid states in UI flow (missing params, session error, etc.)

## PostHog Tracking (mandatory for relevant interactions)

- Track user-relevant interactions with `posthog.capture(...)`
- Use event naming: `[resource]_[action]_[context]`
- Add tracking in pages/components where interaction happens
- Never track sensitive data (PII, auth tokens, raw sensitive payloads)

